.TH ZDOTS-WATCH 1 "2026-08-02" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-watch \- Scheduled health detectors. Notifies (macOS) ONLY on worsening transitions;
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-watch --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
Usage: zdots-watch [run|run-check|status|--install|--uninstall|--install-check|--uninstall-check]

Scheduled health detectors. Notifies (macOS) ONLY on worsening transitions;
improvements and steady state update the state files silently.
  doctor loop : new [FAIL]/[warn] or more capability contract errors (/Users/mike.hall/.local/state/zsh/zdots-watch.state)
  suite loop  : new failing bin/check test, by NAME (/Users/mike.hall/.local/state/zsh/zdots-watch-check.state)

Commands:
  run               one doctor cycle + notify-on-worsening (what launchd calls)
  run-check         one bin/check cycle + notify-on-new-failure (nightly launchd)
  status            show last recorded state + LaunchAgent load status (default)
  --install         render + load the doctor LaunchAgent (every 86400s; plist
                    rendered with live paths at install time — never tracked)
  --uninstall       unload + remove the doctor LaunchAgent
  --install-check   render + load the nightly suite LaunchAgent (daily at 3:17)
  --uninstall-check unload + remove the suite LaunchAgent
  -h, --help        show this help

Knobs: ZDOTS_WATCH_INTERVAL (seconds, default 86400),
       ZDOTS_WATCH_CHECK_HOUR (default 3), ZDOTS_WATCH_CHECK_CMD (test seam),
       ZDOTS_WATCH_KEEP (evidence files kept per detector, default 7).
Evidence: full run output persisted under /Users/mike.hall/.local/state/zsh/zdots-watch-runs
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
